SUBDEEP.update({
"alaska-senate-certification-lawsuit":dict(intro="<b>The U.S. Justice Department has filed a federal lawsuit asking a court to stop Alaska from certifying its Nov 3 U.S. Senate result in one specific case:</b> if incumbent Republican Sen. Dan S. Sullivan loses, and the votes cast for a second candidate, Daniel J. Sullivan, would have been enough to change the outcome under Alaska's ranked choice count. The suit was filed late Thursday, October 22, AP reports. The race pits Sen. Sullivan against Democrat Mary Peltola.",
facts=[("Filed","Late Thu Oct 22, 2026, U.S. District Court for the District of Alaska"),("Plaintiff","The United States, represented by the Attorney General"),("Defendants","The State of Alaska and state election officials"),("What it asks","No certification if Sen. Sullivan loses and the Daniel J. Sullivan votes could have flipped the ranked choice result"),("The second candidate","Daniel J. Sullivan, who filed on or about May 29, 2026, per the complaint"),("June 15 decision","The Alaska Division of Elections found his candidacy was not filed in good faith"),("Courts","Alaska courts later ruled he could stay on the ballot (NBC News)"),("Ballot labels","Dan S. Sullivan is listed as registered Republican and incumbent (NBC News)"),("Election Day","Tue Nov 3, 2026")],
body=f'''<h2>What the lawsuit argues</h2><p>The complaint argues that the second Sullivan's candidacy could confuse voters who mean to back the senator, and that Alaska should not certify a result that may be affected by that confusion. The Justice Department's filing quotes the June 15 finding by the Alaska Division of Elections, which said the declaration of candidacy was filed to confuse or mislead voters.</p>
<h2>The other side of the story</h2><p>Alaska's own courts ruled that Daniel J. Sullivan could stay on the ballot after the Division of Elections tried to remove him, NBC News reports, and the ballot labels the incumbent as the registered Republican and incumbent. AP notes that many fear the case could become a lengthy fight between the federal government and states over certifying elections. President Trump told reporters on Friday, "I'm the one that said do it," per AP.</p>
<h2>What happens next</h2><p>A federal judge will decide whether the case moves forward and whether to grant any order. Voting continues as normal, and Election Day is Tuesday, November 3. No ruling had been reported when we checked on October 24. We will update this page with court filings as they come in, and we link the full complaint below so you can read it yourself.</p>
<p class="warn">Strictly nonpartisan: we summarize the filings and reporting from both sides and never endorse candidates or parties.</p>
<h2>Keep reading</h2><ul><li><a href="../elections-2026/">Elections 2026: the races to watch</a></li><li><a href="../early-voting-2026/">Early voting by state</a></li><li><a href="{R2}blog/midterms-2026-explained/">The midterms, explained without the spin</a></li><li><a href="../government-shutdown-deadline-2026/">The Dec 11 government funding deadline</a></li><li><a href="../supreme-court/">Supreme Court watch</a></li></ul>'''+follow("Alaska"),
faq=[("Why is the Justice Department suing Alaska?","It argues that a second Senate candidate named Daniel J. Sullivan could mislead voters who intend to vote for Sen. Dan S. Sullivan, and it wants certification blocked if those votes could have changed the result."),("Does the lawsuit stop people from voting in Alaska?","No. It targets certification after the election, not voting. Election Day is November 3, 2026."),("Who is running for Senate in Alaska in 2026?","The main contenders are Republican Sen. Dan S. Sullivan and Democrat Mary Peltola. Daniel J. Sullivan is also on the ballot."),("Why is Daniel J. Sullivan still on the ballot?","Alaska election officials removed him in June, finding his candidacy was not in good faith, but Alaska courts ruled he could stay on, NBC News reports."),("Has a judge ruled on the Alaska certification lawsuit?","No ruling had been reported as of October 24, 2026. The suit was filed late on October 22.")]),
"four-corners-flooding-2026":dict(intro="<b>Flash flooding swept across the Four Corners on October 22 and 23, 2026.</b> In Pagosa Springs, Colorado, the San Juan River peaked just over 15 feet around 5:30 a.m. Friday and then began to fall, the Pagosa Springs Sun reports, but mandatory evacuations stayed in place for flood-prone areas. Arizona saw helicopter rescues, southern Utah is cleaning up, and forecasters warn more rain could fall this weekend.",
facts=[("When","Wed Oct 22 to Fri Oct 23, 2026"),("States hit","Colorado, Utah, Arizona, New Mexico"),("San Juan River crest","Just over 15 ft at the Pagosa Springs gauge, about 5:30 a.m. Fri"),("Evacuations","Mandatory, low-lying areas along the San Juan, Rio Blanco, Navajo and Piedra rivers"),("Schools","Archuleta School District closed Fri Oct 23"),("Major closures","US 160 Wolf Creek Pass, US 550 Red Mountain Pass, CO 17, CO 151 (CDOT, Oct 23 8 a.m.)"),("Utah","About 80 homes affected in Hurricane (NBC News)"),("Arizona","4 people rescued by helicopter south of Sedona (NBC News)"),("Alerts","Archuleta County Nixle: text 81147 to 888777")],
body=f'''<h2>Colorado</h2><p>The Town of Pagosa Springs says floodwaters may contain untreated sewage after three wastewater lift stations and one pump station were inundated, so stay out of the water. Hot Springs Boulevard is closed at the bridge, and Town Hall, the Community Center and the Visitor Center are closed through the weekend. The Colorado Department of Transportation is urging drivers to avoid travel in the flood watch areas and never to drive around closure gates. Check <a href="https://www.cotrip.org/" {EXT}>COtrip.org</a> before you go anywhere.</p>
<h2>Utah, Arizona and New Mexico</h2><p>In Hurricane, Utah, a shipping container drifted down a street before the cleanup began, AP reports, and flood watches shifted to southeast Utah into the weekend. In Arizona, four people were lifted off the roof of a vehicle by helicopter south of Sedona, NBC News reported, and northern New Mexico saw evacuations and roof rescues.</p>
<h2>Stay safe</h2><ol><li><b>Turn around, don't drown.</b> Just a little moving water can sweep a car away.</li><li><b>Sign up for local alerts</b> (Nixle, your county's emergency page) and follow evacuation orders.</li><li><b>Stay away from riverbanks</b> even as water drops, because the ground is saturated.</li></ol>
<h2>Keep reading</h2><ul><li><a href="{R2}blog/four-corners-flooding-explained/">Our explainer: why the Southwest is flooding in October</a></li><li><a href="../fall/">Fall 2026 weather watch</a></li><li><a href="../santa-ana-fire-watch/">Santa Ana fire watch</a></li><li><a href="{R2}news/">Today's news buzz</a></li></ul>'''+follow("COwx"),
faq=[("Where is the flooding in the Four Corners?","Southwest and south-central Colorado (including Pagosa Springs), southern Utah, northern Arizona and northern New Mexico, on October 22 and 23, 2026."),("How high did the San Juan River get in Pagosa Springs?","It peaked just over 15 feet at the Pagosa Springs gauge around 5:30 a.m. on Friday, October 23, then started to recede, per the Pagosa Springs Sun."),("Is Wolf Creek Pass open?","CDOT listed US 160 over Wolf Creek Pass as closed as of 8 a.m. on October 23. Check COtrip.org for the latest."),("Will it rain more in the Four Corners this weekend?","Forecasters say more heavy rain is possible this weekend, and flood watches were in effect in southeast Utah, per AP."),("How do I get flood alerts in Archuleta County?","Text 81147 to 888777 to sign up for Nixle alerts, the county's main emergency channel.")]),
"nairobi-building-collapse-2026":dict(intro="<b>A multistorey building under construction collapsed in Nairobi's busy Eastleigh district</b> at about 1 p.m. local time on <b>Friday, October 23, 2026</b>. Kenya's interior minister said 67 workers were on site, with one injured and 66 unharmed, and rescuers reported contact with some survivors still trapped, Al Jazeera, AP and AFP report. People in shops on the lower floors were still unaccounted for.",
facts=[("When","Fri Oct 23, 2026, about 1 p.m. local (10:00 GMT)"),("Where","Eastleigh, Nairobi, Kenya"),("Workers on site","67: 66 unharmed, 1 injured (Interior Minister Kipchumba Murkomen)"),("Missing","About 11 people in ground-floor shops were unaccounted for on Friday; Daily Nation later reported seven missing"),("Status of building","Approved for construction but no occupation certificate, per Governor Johnson Sakaja"),("Police","A search for the building's owner was launched (Nairobi police chief)"),("Rescue","Government, county and Kenya Red Cross teams; work continued overnight into Saturday")],
body=f'''<h2>What officials said</h2><p>Nairobi Governor Johnson Sakaja said the shops on the ground floor should not have been open because the building had no occupation certificate. "Our concern is to save lives," he told reporters, per Al Jazeera. Police warned of a possible second collapse because the structure was leaning on its neighbor.</p>
<h2>Why it matters</h2><p>Kenya's National Building Inspectorate found that 87 percent of buildings audited nationwide last year failed to meet standards or lacked approvals, AFP reported. Officials said anyone found negligent would face the law. Numbers often change in the first days after a collapse, so rely on official updates and wire services.</p>
<h2>Keep reading</h2><ul><li><a href="../">What's trending in world news</a></li><li><a href="../tibet-earthquake-2026/">Tibet earthquake updates</a></li><li><a href="../ebola-outbreak-2026/">Ebola outbreak tracker</a></li><li><a href="{R2}news/">Today's news buzz</a></li></ul>'''+follow("Eastleigh"),
faq=[("What happened in Eastleigh, Nairobi?","A multistorey building under construction collapsed on Friday, October 23, 2026, at about 1 p.m. local time."),("How many people are missing in the Nairobi building collapse?","About 11 people in ground-floor shops were unaccounted for on Friday, per Al Jazeera. Kenya's Daily Nation later reported seven missing. Figures may change."),("Was anyone rescued from the Nairobi collapse?","Yes. The Kenya Red Cross said two injured people were rescued and taken to Kenyatta National Hospital, per local reports cited by Al Jazeera."),("Why were people inside a building under construction?","Officials say the ground floor and basement had been rented to shops even though the building had no occupation certificate, which the governor said made it illegal.")]),
})
