_ws["intro"]="<b>The Milwaukee Brewers lead the World Series 1-0</b> after holding off the Tampa Bay Rays 3-2 in Game 1 on Friday night. Christian Yelich tripled in the first run, and Trevor Megill struck out Jonny DeLuca with two runners in scoring position to end it, after a replay review overturned what was first called a game-ending double play, AP reports. <b>Game 2 is tonight, Saturday, October 24, at 8 p.m. ET</b> in Milwaukee on FOX: Logan Henderson for the Brewers against Drew Rasmussen for the Rays."
_ws["facts"]=[("Series","Brewers lead 1-0, best of seven"),("Game 1, Oct 23","Brewers 3, Rays 2. W: Jacob Misiorowski. L: Nick Martinez. S: Trevor Megill"),("Game 2","Tonight, Sat Oct 24, 8 p.m. ET, American Family Field (FOX, FOX Deportes, FOX One)"),("Game 2 starters","Logan Henderson (MIL) vs. Drew Rasmussen (TB)"),("Game 3","Mon Oct 26, 8 p.m. ET, at Rays"),("Game 4","Tue Oct 27, 8 p.m. ET, at Rays"),("Game 5 (if needed)","Wed Oct 28, at Rays"),("Games 6 and 7 (if needed)","Fri Oct 30 and Sat Oct 31, at Brewers"),("Regular season","Brewers 103 wins, Rays 97"),("Title history","Neither franchise has won a World Series")]
_ws["faq"]=[("Who won Game 1 of the 2026 World Series?","The Milwaukee Brewers beat the Tampa Bay Rays 3-2 on October 23, 2026, at American Family Field."),("When is World Series Game 2?","Saturday, October 24, 2026, at 8 p.m. ET in Milwaukee, on FOX, FOX Deportes and FOX One."),("Who is pitching Game 2 of the World Series?","Logan Henderson for Milwaukee and Drew Rasmussen for Tampa Bay, per MLB.com and NBC Sports."),("What happened at the end of World Series Game 1?","A game-ending double play was overturned on replay because shortstop Cooper Pratt's foot was off the bag, a run scored, and then Trevor Megill struck out Jonny DeLuca to finish the 3-2 win, AP reports."),("Have the Brewers or Rays ever won the World Series?","No. Milwaukee lost its only previous World Series in 1982, and Tampa Bay lost in 2008 and 2020."),("When would World Series Game 7 be?","If needed, Saturday, October 31, 2026, in Milwaukee.")]
_ws["body"]=f'''<h2>How Game 1 played out</h2><p>Milwaukee jumped out early: Yelich's triple scored Jackson Chourio and William Contreras singled home Yelich in the first. Tampa Bay got one back in the fourth, and Chourio's RBI single made it 3-1 in the seventh. In the ninth the Rays loaded the bases with a double steal and a walk, and Liam Hicks' grounder was ruled a game-ending double play until replay showed Cooper Pratt's foot was slightly off the bag. Megill then struck out DeLuca. The Rays went 0 for 6 with runners in scoring position, while Jonathan Aranda reached base four times, per AP.</p>
<h2>Game 2 tonight</h2><p>Logan Henderson starts for Milwaukee and Drew Rasmussen, who began his career in the Brewers organization, starts for Tampa Bay. First pitch is 8 p.m. ET on FOX. Our <a href="{R2}blog/world-series-game-2-2026-tonight/">Game 2 cheat sheet</a> has everything in one place, and the <a href="{R2}blog/rays-brewers-world-series-2026-preview/">series preview</a> covers both rosters.</p>
<p>Also today: <a href="../wnba-finals-2026/">WNBA Finals Game 4 at 1 p.m. ET</a> and the <a href="../nfl/">NFL Week 8 schedule</a>.</p>'''+follow("WorldSeries")
